# No line-ending translation anywhere under experiments/.
#
# SHA256SUMS is computed over the bytes of these files. If Git translated LF to CRLF on
# checkout — which it does by default on Windows — every checksum would fail on a platform
# other than the one that generated them, and a reviewer would be unable to tell a real
# corruption from a line-ending artefact. The files are stored and checked out verbatim.
* -text
